Code and design reused under the MIT License
--------------------------------------------

* Linuity - https://github.com/gabrielvictorweb/linuity
  Copyright (c) Gabriel Victor and contributors. MIT License (as declared in
  its README).
  Used for: the layered architecture (ports / use cases / infrastructure /
  presentation); the skeleton of the GTK 4 interface (header bar, stack
  switcher, "already applied" button, log viewer through journalctl); the
  daemon loop with reconnection; log formatting (infra/logging_config.py);
  atomic writes of settings and presets; the blink, gradual, flicker, scanner
  and wave effects (generalized to per-key RGB); the structure of install.sh.

* PlasmaNGenuity - https://github.com/radoslavchobanov/plasmangenuity
  Copyright (c) Radoslav Chobanov and contributors. MIT License (as declared in
  its README, pyproject.toml and PKGBUILD).
  Used for: the driver registry with match(vid, pid, interface); the
  Capabilities / DeviceInfo model; JSON configuration with defaults and deep
  merge; the separation between a pure protocol module (no I/O) and the
  driver.

* hyperx-studio - https://github.com/Shehtman/hyperx-studio
  MIT License. (It targets the full-size Alloy Origins; its protocol is NOT
  used.) Ideas adapted and rewritten in Python: system audio capture through
  parec / pw-record with Goertzel bands, automatic gain and beat detection; the
  equalizer, sound spectrum, sound pulse and music wave effects; the fire and
  snake effects (redone to loop, so they can be written to onboard memory); a
  key-press reaction layer on top of any effect; not re-sending identical
  frames; releasing the keyboard before system sleep (systemd-sleep hook and
  USBDEVFS_RESET).

